.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_STREAM_ERROR 3 "2026-10-01" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_stream_error \- report why the last chttpsvr_req_read call failed
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_req_stream_error(const chttpsvr_req *req);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Reports why the last chttpsvr_req_read call on req returned -1.  The
result is meaningful only immediately after such a -1 return and is
unspecified at any other time.

It distinguishes only the genuine, data-dependent transfer errors of
chttpsvr_req_read (see chttpsvr_req_read(3)).  When caller misuse
caused the -1 instead, it reports ccol_success, which you cannot tell
apart from "no error".  Two kinds of misuse cause this: buf was NULL
while buflen was above 0, or the route of the request was not
registered with chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler.  Both are static
programming errors that happen on every call to the faulty code, not
only sometimes, so a caller that hits one is expected to find and fix
it in ordinary testing rather than diagnose it at run time.

Return values:
  ccol_timed_out             stream_read_timeout_us expired while the
                              handler waited for the next batch; or
                              the total body read time of the request
                              exceeded max_body_read_duration_us, when
                              that field is set; or the average rate
                              of the body fell below
                              min_transfer_rate_bps after the grace
                              period.
  ccol_msg_too_large         The body exceeded max_body_size
                              mid-stream, or the declared size of one
                              chunk of a chunked Transfer-Encoding
                              exceeded max_body_size before the server
                              read any data of that chunk.
  ccol_not_enough_memory     An internal allocation failed while the
                              server grew the body buffer; the client
                              did not cause this.
  ccol_http_transfer_aborted The connection was closed or reset, or
                              the framing of the body was malformed.
  ccol_success               There is no error on record for req, or
                              one of the misuse cases above caused
                              the -1.
  ccol_unexpected_failure    req is NULL, or its handle is invalid.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_read (3),
.BR chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler (3)
